                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I would like to know if there's going to be future updates for this game. It nails a whole lot of areas that other games don't. But it's just not a \"polished\" game and without early access status. Interesting! But I might wait for an update before deciding on this.\n\nPicture Space Pirate Trainer as a fantasy/medival wave shooter with more than a 3 lives per game limit (it's much more.) Creatures will attack you and it appears that that's OK as you can handle the damage. The 3d models and the various monsters are better than most and welcomed compared to just drone fighting. I had some video jitter issues on a 2600k, 1080 nvidia, 16gb system. The weapons are cool but it doesn't feel like you \"own\" the weapons like you do in SPT. But this is the polish I'm referring to.\n\nI did want to stop playing it early due to the stuttering. Here's to hoping!\n\nUpdate:\nI played this game again for the same amount of time I played it before. Here's my impressions:\n\n- You get overrun by monsters invading your personal space. It's alittle annoying.\n- It's not worth the money. And that could be deamed with a \"yet\". Needs polish. Lots of it.\n- Stutters like no tomorrow on a 1080.  Did not see a settings option.\n- I still hate the audio cues like \"Monsters is coming!\"\n- Devs need to focus on game play and performance. \n- I probably wont play this again unless notified the game was updated.\n- If there were RPG elements in the game like updating the weapons, I did not see them.\n- When you die you just start over.\n- Guns are lame, swords are ok and bow is pretty cool.\n- I spent more time on this review than playing the game.",
